rd\",\n        \"grounded_content\": \"Record pinned Arena/NBA sources, content-group split, largest connected components, NBA copy filtering and historical team-code limitations, source/payload hashes, declared seeds, CPU dependencies and staged-resource commands from inspected manifests/code. Distinguish protocol metadata from measured findings. A complete raw-to-partition builder and all original raw archives are not staged; do not claim otherwise.\",\n        \"source_ids\": [\n          \"final.evidence.episodes\",\n          \"final.qualification.status\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"heading\": \"Numerical and row-order checks\",\n        \"grounded_content\": \"Explain residual tolerances, no-deletion zero disruption, invalid constant-certificate rejection, reversed-row invariance, and unverified candidate-authored diagnostics. Preserve the exact final qualification outcome without inferring undocumented gate causes or generalization.\",\n        \"source_ids\": [\n          \"final.evidence.episodes\",\n          \"final.qualification.status\",\n          \"final.qualification.outcome\",\n          \"final.qualification.correct\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"heading\": \"Descriptive search configurations\",\n        \"grounded_content\": \"Archive raw scores and inspected implementations for clean-Hessian selection, bounded exact refits and retained-curvature expansion. State missing final controlled ablations and selection-adjusted uncertainty. A tied aggregate is not identical behavior or an overhead measurement. Do not report campaign counts, unscored losses, derived search deltas, or original-starter performance without study.* sources.\",\n        \"source_ids\": [\n          \"result.top_program_01\",\n          \"result.top_program_02\",\n          \"result.top_program_03\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"heading\": \"Conditional uncertainty protocol and stored records\",\n        \"grounded_content\": \"Give the complete unique group-weight records and bootstrap algorithm; masks are fixed, weighted removed mass varies, and selection is not rerun. Contrast this with aggregate seed-resampling intervals and their deterministic degeneracy. The main text retains opposite high-loss-relative signs and the conditioning limitations.\",\n        \"source_ids\": [\n          \"final.evidence.episodes\",\n          \"final.metric.paired_gain_disagreement_ci_low\",\n          \"final.metric.paired_gain_disagreement_ci_high\",\n          \"final.metric.paired_gain_random_ci_low\",\n          \"final.metric.paired_gain_random_ci_high\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"heading\": \"LLM Usage\",\n        \"grounded_content\": \"Disclose the roles documented in supplied agent-run logs and artifacts: research ideation, candidate-code generation, reference-query planning, and manuscript assistance. Distinguish these from the numerical evaluator. Do not invent provider/model identities, human oversight or paid-API experiments; this is process provenance, not a numerical result.\",\n        \"source_ids\": []\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"forbidden_headings\": [\n\n---MEMO TARGET---\n21:This is fresh framing, not an edit pass: no resolved edit-context files, previous_paper, aggregated, extra_tasks, or prior manuscript are staged. The status means recentering the source-task brief, not editing an unseen paper. Compare three alternatives: preserving the proposed dependence-aware, multi-judge frontier story is unsupported; broadening to a universal cross-design robustness method overstates unmatched evidence; centering the shared frozen-prefix row-deletion audit and heterogeneous measured limits is supported. Method detail and figure density are not reasons to preserve an unsupported story.\n23:Prior-story status: **recentered** (source-brief recentering; no prior manuscript was staged).\n29:- results/best_program_manifest.json identifies the six-contender exact-refit configuration. Its inspected source supports the named method family; final provenance records a program-tree digest, but an independent reconstruction of that digest is not claimed.\n127:- Layout justification: Two panels across the full 5.5-inch text block leave room for 32 observations per dataset, explicit comparator titles, zero reference, and labels at least 9 pt. Use reproducible display jitter, not more statistical samples.\n131:## Supplementary plan\n132:Provide implementation, provenance, numerical-control, and uncertainty depth needed to reproduce and audit the narrow claim, without moving the decisive contrasts or limitations out of the main paper.\n139:### Data partitioning and reproducibility record\n140:Record pinned Arena/NBA sources, content-group split, largest connected components, NBA copy filtering and historical team-code limitations, source/payload hashes, declared seeds, CPU dependencies and staged-resource commands from inspected manifests/code. Distinguish protocol metadata from measured findings. A complete raw-to-partition builder and all original raw archives are not staged; do not claim otherwise.\n150:Archive raw scores and inspected implementations for clean-Hessian selection, bounded exact refits and retained-curvature expansion. State missing final controlled ablations and selection-adjusted uncertainty. A tied aggregate is not identical behavior or an overhead measurement. Do not report campaign counts, unscored losses, derived search deltas, or original-starter performance without study.* sources.\n159:### LLM Usage\n162:Grounding IDs: process provenance only; no numerical source ID claimed.\n166:1. Scope: this strategy writes neither paper.tex nor claims_grounding.json, drafts no final paper, renders no figures, runs no new experiment, and invokes no final-paper validation. Dotted JSON fields, internal selection terms and hashes in this memo are private-only source maps, not visible manuscript labels. Memory is qualitative planning context only.\n186:11. Qualification: current authoritative final sources report completed and qualified. This does not establish generalization or universal superiority. If later authoritative evidence reports failed qualification, disclose and preserve it through writing, review, audit and revision; distinguish statistical/performance causes from validity/adaptivity causes only when identified by evaluator diagnostics. Missing causes stay unknown.\n188:12. Source map: final.evidence.episodes supports per-case data and conditional resampling; final.metric.* supports aggregate metrics; final.qualification.* alone grounds qualification. No downstream_study or study.* sources exist, so omit campaign selection advantages, derived search-score differences, attempt counts and original-starter quantitative comparison. Use result.top_program_* only for clearly labeled descriptive raw search scores. Unscored performance is missing, not a loss.\n194:15. Figure outputs: quantitative plots require reproducible source, vector PDF and 300-DPI PNG. LaTeX must reference PDF whenever it exists. Prefer editable draw.io plus PDF/PNG for the concept overview; if raster-only, require at least 2400 px width for these full-width figures, or 1200 px for any later justified column-scale raster. Regenerate rather than upscale. Follow concept-figure orchestration later; do not render during strategy generation.\n198:17. Supplement: substantive material already exists. After references use a clear page, appendix mode, and Supplementary Information in the same paper source; include a separate LLM Usage subsection. Authoritative posthoc rankings arrive separately; route appendix-ranked analyses there without guessing rankings now or moving central evidence out of the main text.\n200:18. Anonymity: omit names, affiliations, acknowledgements, funding, self-identifying links and internal URLs. Remove template final-copy/author scaffolding during drafting while preserving its required watermark. Include the separate LLM Usage disclosure; do not invent a mandatory checklist not supplied for this venue.\n202:19. Reproducibility: inspected sources include the candidate, evaluator, normalized resources/manifests and numpy==2.2.6, scipy==1.15.3 requirements. A complete raw-to-partition builder and all raw originals are not staged. Inventory actual available artifacts/commands and distinguish staged-resource reruns from raw-source reconstruction. Do not claim the broader reproduction package is already complete.\n210:These lists prohibit chronology framing, unsupported claims, and pipeline-native visible labels; source identifiers elsewhere in this strategy are private-only grounding, not exceptions.\n\n---DATA SHAPE---\nRoot keys: ['ablation_studies', 'all_programs', 'best_any', 'best_correct', 'evidence_sources', 'final_evaluation', 'generated_at', 'grounding_sources', 'idea_titles', 'improvement_trace', 'paper_profile', 'presentation_contract', 'results_dir', 'top_programs', 'totals']\nFinal evaluation: ['correct', 'evaluation_evidence', 'evaluator_sha256', 'manifest_path', 'metrics', 'outcome', 'program_tree_sha256', 'results_tree_sha256', 'status', 'task_tree_sha256']\nSources type: NoneType\n\n---VALIDATION SCRIPTS---\n.codex/skills/memory-log/scripts/append_memory.py\n../paper/strategy_validation_feedback.json\n../paper/strategy_validation_feedback.md\n.codex/skills/write-paper-standalone/templates/alife/paper.tex\n.codex/skills/write-paper-standalone/templates/iclr/paper.tex\n\n---GEOMETRY---\n48:\\textheight 9.0 true in       % Height of text (including footnotes & figures)\n49:\\textwidth 5.5 true in        % Width of text line.\n83:\\def\\@maketitle{\\vbox{\\hsize\\textwidth\n170:% Less leading in most fonts (due to the narrow columns)\n186:\\def\\bottomtitlebar{\\vskip .29in\\vskip-\\parskip\\hrule height1pt\\vskip\n187:.09in} %\n215:\\textheight=#5\\vbadness=10000\\vfuzz=120ex\\overfullrule=0pt%\n216:\\global\\setbox\\iclrrulerbox=\\vbox to \\textheight{%\n217:{\\parskip=0pt\\hfuzz=150em\\cv@boxheight=\\textheight\n229:\\def\\iclrruler#1{\\makevruler[12pt][#1][1][3][0.993\\textheight]\\usebox{\\iclrrulerbox}}\n232:\\iclrruleroffset=\\textheight\n245:% \\colorbox[rgb]{0.7,0.7,0.7}{\\small \\parbox[b][\\textheight]{0.1cm}{}}}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
