{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"printf '\\\\n---SOURCE CATALOG---\\\\n'; jq '.grounding_sources|type' paper_data.json; jq '.grounding_sources|if type==\\\"object\\\" then keys else .[0:3] end' paper_data.json; printf '\\\\n---EVIDENCE CATALOG---\\\\n'; jq '.evidence_sources|if type==\\\"object\\\" then keys else .[0:2] end' paper_data.json; printf '\\\\n---FINAL QUALIFICATION---\\\\n'; jq '.final_evaluation|{status,outcome,correct}' paper_data.json; printf '\\\\n---TARGET MEMO---\\\\n'; sed -n '123,165p' paper_strategy.md; printf '\\\\n---HELPER LOCATIONS---\\\\n'; ls /usr/local/bin /tmp /opt /workspace | head -70; printf '\\\\n---TEMPLATE---\\\\n'; sed -n '1,75p' .codex/skills/write-paper-standalone/templates/iclr/paper.tex; printf '\\\\n---STRATEGY TOP---\\\\n'; sed -n '1,70p' paper_strategy.json\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"printf '\\\\n---SOURCE CATALOG---\\\\n'; jq '.grounding_sources|type' paper_data.json; jq '.grounding_sources|if type==\\\"object\\\" then keys else .[0:3] end' paper_data.json; printf '\\\\n---EVIDENCE CATALOG---\\\\n'; jq '.evidence_sources|if type==\\\"object\\\" then keys else .[0:2] end' paper_data.json; printf '\\\\n---FINAL QUALIFICATION---\\\\n'; jq '.final_evaluation|{status,outcome,correct}' paper_data.json; printf '\\\\n---TARGET MEMO---\\\\n'; sed -n '123,165p' paper_strategy.md; printf '\\\\n---HELPER LOCATIONS---\\\\n'; ls /usr/local/bin /tmp /opt /workspace | head -70; printf '\\\\n---TEMPLATE---\\\\n'; sed -n '1,75p' .codex/skills/write-paper-standalone/templates/iclr/paper.tex; printf '\\\\n---STRATEGY TOP---\\\\n'; sed -n '1,70p' paper_strategy.json\"","aggregated_output":"[\n  \"ablations\",\n  \"investigation\"\n]\n\n---FINAL QUALIFICATION---\n{\n  \"status\": \"completed\",\n  \"outcome\": \"qualified\",\n  \"correct\": true\n}\n\n---TARGET MEMO---\n- Placement: Immediately after Figure 2, approximately page 6 or 7; never supplementary-only. Width: 1.0 of text width (full_width).\n\n- Footprint: About 0.65 page including caption; artwork about 2.7 inches tall.\n\n- Layout justification: Two panels across the full 5.5-inch text block leave room for 32 observations per dataset, explicit comparator titles, zero reference, and labels at least 9 pt. Use reproducible display jitter, not more statistical samples.\n\n- Grounding IDs: `final.evidence.episodes`. Supporting protocol/implementation: `task/evaluate_final.py:final_uncertainty`.\n\n## Supplementary plan\nProvide implementation, provenance, numerical-control, and uncertainty depth needed to reproduce and audit the narrow claim, without moving the decisive contrasts or limitations out of the main paper.\n\n### Retained-mean objective and frozen-prefix selection\nExpand centered ridge Bradley–Terry, half-win ties, clean contrast/influence solves, retained-mean displacement correction, deterministic tie rules, six-contender selection, pair-statistic compression, warm starts/cache, convergence tolerances, incomplete-refit fallback, and selector/evaluation metric mismatch. Inspected program.py, IMPLEMENTATION.md, and evaluator explain the mechanism, not unreported internal shortlist decisions.\n\nGrounding IDs: `final.evidence.episodes`.\n\n### Data partitioning and reproducibility record\nRecord pinned Arena/NBA sources, content-group split, largest connected components, NBA copy filtering and historical team-code limitations, source/payload hashes, declared seeds, CPU dependencies and staged-resource commands from inspected manifests/code. Distinguish protocol metadata from measured findings. A complete raw-to-partition builder and all original raw archives are not staged; do not claim otherwise.\n\nGrounding IDs: `final.evidence.episodes`, `final.qualification.status`.\n\n### Numerical and row-order checks\nExplain residual tolerances, no-deletion zero disruption, invalid constant-certificate rejection, reversed-row invariance, and unverified candidate-authored diagnostics. Preserve the exact final qualification outcome without inferring undocumented gate causes or generalization.\n\nGrounding IDs: `final.evidence.episodes`, `final.qualification.status`, `final.qualification.outcome`, `final.qualification.correct`.\n\n### Descriptive search configurations\nArchive raw scores and inspected implementations for clean-Hessian selection, bounded exact refits and retained-curvature expansion. State missing final controlled ablations and selection-adjusted uncertainty. A tied aggregate is not identical behavior or an overhead measurement. Do not report campaign counts, unscored losses, derived search deltas, or original-starter performance without study.* sources.\n\nGrounding IDs: `result.top_program_01`, `result.top_program_02`, `result.top_program_03`.\n\n### Conditional uncertainty protocol and stored records\nGive the complete unique group-weight records and bootstrap algorithm; masks are fixed, weighted removed mass varies, and selection is not rerun. Contrast this with aggregate seed-resampling intervals and their deterministic degeneracy. The main text retains opposite high-loss-relative signs and the conditioning limitations.\n\nGrounding IDs: `final.evidence.episodes`, `final.metric.paired_gain_disagreement_ci_low`, `final.metric.paired_gain_disagreement_ci_high`, `final.metric.paired_gain_random_ci_low`, `final.metric.paired_gain_random_ci_high`.\n\n### LLM Usage\nDisclose the roles documented in supplied agent-run logs and artifacts: research ideation, candidate-code generation, reference-query planning, and manuscript assistance. Distinguish these from the numerical evaluator. Do not invent provider/model identities, human oversight or paid-API experiments; this is process provenance, not a numerical result.\n\nGrounding IDs: process provenance only; no numerical source ID claimed.\n\n## Writer contract: body budget, output, and limitations\n\n\n---HELPER LOCATIONS---\n/opt:\nautoillustrate-venv\ndrawio\nheadless\n\n/tmp:\nnode-compile-cache\nopencode\n\n/usr/local/bin:\n2to3\n2to3-3.12\nautoillustrate\nclaude\ncodex\ndocutils\ndotenv\ndrawio\ngemini\nheadless\nhttpx\nidle\nidle3\nidle3.12\nidna\nlatex2text\nlatexencode\nlatexwalker\nnode\nnormalizer\nnpm\nnpx\nopencode\npi\npip\npip3\npip3.12\npybabel\npydoc\npydoc3\npydoc3.12\npygmentize\npython\npython-config\npython3\npython3-config\npython3.12\npython3.12-config\nrst2html\nrst2html4\nrst2html5\nrst2latex\nrst2man\nrst2odt\nrst2pseudoxml\nrst2s5\nrst2xetex\nrst2xml\nsphinx-apidoc\nsphinx-autogen\nsphinx-build\nsphinx-quickstart\nwsdump\n\n/workspace:\nfinal_evaluation\ninvestigation\nmetrics\npaper\npipeline_events.jsonl\n\n---TEMPLATE---\n\\documentclass{article}\n% --- watermark (auto-inserted) ---\n\\usepackage{xcolor}\n\\usepackage{xfp}% \\fpeval; in the kernel since 2022, harmless on older LaTeX\n\\usepackage{draftwatermark}\n\\newlength{\\watermarkTextWidth}\n\\AddToHook{begindocument/end}{%\n  \\SetWatermarkText{\\normalfont Generated by The Agentic Scientist}%\n  \\SetWatermarkFontSize{10pt}%\n  \\SetWatermarkLightness{0.85}%\n  \\settowidth{\\watermarkTextWidth}{\\normalfont\\fontsize{10pt}{12pt}\\selectfont Generated by The Agentic Scientist}%\n  \\edef\\watermarkScale{\\fpeval{0.8 * sqrt(\\paperwidth**2 + \\paperheight**2) / \\watermarkTextWidth}}%\n  \\edef\\watermarkAngle{\\fpeval{atand(\\paperheight/\\paperwidth)}}%\n  \\SetWatermarkScale{\\watermarkScale}%\n  \\SetWatermarkAngle{\\watermarkAngle}%\n}\n% --- end watermark ---\n % For LaTeX2e\n\\usepackage{paper,times}\n\n\\usepackage{hyperref}\n\\usepackage{url}\n\n\\title{Grounded Experimental Summary}\n\\iclrfinalcopy\n\\author{The Agentic Scientist}\n\n\\begin{document}\n\\maketitle\n\n\\begin{abstract}\nReplace with a concise grounded abstract summarizing setup, core result, and takeaway.\n\\end{abstract}\n\n\\section{Introduction}\nReplace with grounded motivation, problem framing, and contributions.\n\n\\section{Related Work}\nSummarize relevant prior work using citation keys present in references.bib (for example, \\citep{templateReference2026}).\n\n\\section{Method}\nDescribe data, setup, and method details needed for reproducibility.\n\n\\section{Results}\nReport grounded quantitative and qualitative findings. Include figures and tables when useful.\n\n\\section{Conclusion}\nState key findings, limitations, and next steps supported by evidence.\n\n% IMPORTANT: \\clearpage flushes all pending floats before references so that\n% body-page counting excludes reference-only pages.  Do NOT remove.\n\\clearpage\n\\bibliography{references}\n\\bibliographystyle{paper}\n\n\\clearpage\n\\appendix\n\\section{Supplementary Information}\n% REQUIRED: Replace this scaffold with substantive grounded content.\n\\subsection{Reproducibility Details}\nReplace with grounded extended methods, reproducibility details, additional analyses, or supporting tables and figures.\n\n\\end{document}\n\n---STRATEGY TOP---\n{\n  \"status\": \"ready\",\n  \"selected_prompt_family\": \"paper_standalone\",\n  \"recommended_title\": \"Exact-Refit Audits of Pairwise Ranking Sensitivity\",\n  \"central_question\": \"How do small, influence-ordered deletions affect regularized Bradley–Terry rankings, and how does their disruption compare with random and high-loss deletion across crowd preferences and historical sports outcomes?\",\n  \"central_thesis\": \"A frozen-prefix audit with bounded exact-refit contender selection yields greater aggregate rank disruption than the measured deletion baselines on the final partitions, but its advantage depends on dataset and deletion budget, with fixed-mask group resampling favoring high-loss deletion in Arena and the studied selector in NBA.\",\n  \"narrative_rationale\": \"The strongest evidence is the direct final comparison on two real-data settings and its conditional uncertainty analysis, not an optimization success story. Use one common sensitivity question with condition-specific evidence blocks, not a causal test of evaluation design. The inspected implementation supports the mechanism description; evaluator refits support measured effectiveness. Search configurations are descriptive supporting material, not independently replicated final ablations. The paper is viable as a bounded empirical audit without universal superiority or novelty-priority claims.\",\n  \"prior_paper_story_status\": \"recentered\",\n  \"edit_framing_decision\": \"This is fresh framing, not an edit pass: no resolved edit-context files, previous_paper, aggregated, extra_tasks, or prior manuscript are staged. The status means recentering the source-task brief, not editing an unseen paper. Compare three alternatives: preserving the proposed dependence-aware, multi-judge frontier story is unsupported; broadening to a universal cross-design robustness method overstates unmatched evidence; centering the shared frozen-prefix row-deletion audit and heterogeneous measured limits is supported. Method detail and figure density are not reasons to preserve an unsupported story.\",\n  \"staged_input_impact\": [\n    \"Read final_evaluation independently: final.qualification.status=completed, final.qualification.outcome=qualified, final.qualification.correct=true. There is no downstream_study or study.* grounding. Qualification is not statistical superiority or generalization; missing additional gate diagnostics remain unknown.\",\n    \"results/best_program_manifest.json identifies the six-contender exact-refit configuration. Its inspected source supports the named method family; final provenance records a program-tree digest, but an independent reconstruction of that digest is not claimed.\",\n    \"Final episodes cover Arena and NBA, not the proposed MT-Bench expert/GPT-4 comparisons. Provenance groups support partitioning and conditional resampling, not whole-group deletion or design labels available to the selector.\",\n    \"Final dataset/budget contrasts and unique fixed-mask bootstrap records shift the thesis away from a general improvement claim. Reversed-row cases are controls, not extra datasets; repeated bootstrap exports are not new resamples.\",\n    \"Clean-Hessian selection and retained-curvature expansion have descriptive search evidence only. No valid grounded metric for the original starter comparator supports retaining its quantitative comparison.\",\n    \"References and provenance include irrelevant retrieval matches and do not resolve all exact planned identities. The bibliography is not evidence of a completed literature review or established novelty.\"\n  ],\n  \"method_groups\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Frozen-prefix bounded exact-refit selector\",\n      \"role\": \"proposed\",\n      \"include_reason\": \"The studied six-contender configuration computes clean influence orders, selects using retained-data refits, and returns frozen nested prefixes for independent evaluation.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Uniform random row deletion\",\n      \"role\": \"baseline\",\n      \"include_reason\": \"Measured at identical floored row budgets; five seeds reflect deletion randomness, not independent dataset draws.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"High-loss row deletion\",\n      \"role\": \"baseline\",\n      \"include_reason\": \"Strong measured comparator ordered by clean per-row Bradley–Terry negative log-likelihood; it is not disagreement between judges. Its Arena advantage is essential.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Unmodified-data and reversed-row controls\",\n      \"role\": \"supporting\",\n      \"include_reason\": \"Numerical zero-change and row-order invariance checks, not reader-facing performance rates or additional replications.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Clean-Hessian-only contender selection\",\n      \"role\": \"ablation\",\n      \"include_reason\": \"Descriptive search-configuration comparison for lookahead, explicitly not a replicated final ablation or causal mechanism attribution.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Retained-curvature shortlist expansion\",\n      \"role\": \"ablation\",\n      \"include_reason\": \"Supporting negative configuration comparison: expanded proxy/exact pools tie the recorded search aggregate. Do not infer identical behavior, equivalence, or efficiency.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"results_focus\": [\n    \"Lead with final dataset-by-budget normalized inversion fractions for the studied selector, high-loss deletion, and random deletion. Use unpermuted cases for performance summaries and reversed-row cases only for invariance checks.\",\n    \"Secondary final aggregate table: studied selector 0.011722185737596697, high-loss deletion 0.009340217174121283, random deletion 0.003902759168170127; paired gains over high-loss and random deletion 0.002381968563475412 and 0.00781942656942657. Sources: final.metric.combined_score, final.metric.disagreement_baseline_score, final.metric.random_baseline_score, final.metric.paired_gain_vs_disagreement, final.metric.paired_gain_vs_random.\",\n    \"Display every unique stored conditional group-bootstrap gain. Each dataset has 32 records, repeated identically across five episode exports, not 160 independent records. All stored high-loss-relative gains are negative in Arena and positive in NBA; Arena random-relative gains include negative observations. Source: final.evidence.episodes.\",\n    \"Separate seed-resampling intervals from group-weight resampling. The high-loss-relative seed interval has equal endpoints because that contrast is deterministic across recorded seeds; it is not certainty about data variation or general superiority.\",\n    \"Use normalized original-leader rank drop 0.03305066318764949 only as a secondary aggregate for the studied selector, grounded in final.metric.mean_leader_rank_drop. Per-budget curves are normalized inversions, not leader drops or minimal reversal budgets.\",\n    \"A small descriptive search table may show raw scores only: clean-Hessian-only selection 0.013240276724865765 (result.top_program_03), bounded exact refits 0.01595532053579999 (result.top_program_01), retained-curvature expansion 0.01595532053579999 (result.top_program_02). Keep this separate from final results; no campaign winner, derived search-delta, or scored/unscored count claims without study.* grounding.\"\n  ],\n  \"figure_plan\": [\n    \"Figure 1: early six-block concept overview of two data settings, shared Bradley–Terry audit, frozen orders, bounded selection, independent refits, and conditional fixed-mask uncertainty.\",\n    \"Figure 2: two dataset panels of grouped dots at three deletion budgets, comparing normalized inversions across the studied selector, high-loss deletion, and random deletion.\",\n    \"Figure 3: two comparator panels showing all unique stored conditional bootstrap gains for Arena and NBA against zero; explicitly fixed masks and no reselection.\"\n  ],\n  \"figure_specs\": [\n    {\n      \"figure_id\": \"audit_overview\",\n      \"required\": true,\n      \"purpose\": \"Give immediate glance value for the common sensitivity object, method, and conditioning boundary.\",\n      \"figure_type\": \"diagram\",\n      \"preferred_generator\": \"generate-concept-figure\",\n      \"group_by\": \"audit_component\",\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
