ee_sha256\": \"sha256:f526616ee82183b25fe4385c172051e1c0ab17259785fe939369b7eff07cf92e\",\n    \"type\": \"final_qualification\",\n    \"value\": \"qualified\"\n  },\n  \"final.qualification.status\": {\n    \"evaluation_scope\": \"sealed_final\",\n    \"id\": \"final.qualification.status\",\n    \"manifest_path\": \"work/results/t06/codex/20261117_205956/final_evaluation/final_manifest.json\",\n    \"program_tree_sha256\": \"sha256:f1de38e95ce991dcd5e4d0053f19985076f23d8691cbfb1c0b835c4884411fc5\",\n    \"results_tree_sha256\": \"sha256:f526616ee82183b25fe4385c172051e1c0ab17259785fe939369b7eff07cf92e\",\n    \"type\": \"final_qualification\",\n    \"value\": \"completed\"\n  }\n}\n\n---MEMO DISCLOSURE---\n### LLM Usage\nDisclose the roles documented in supplied agent-run logs and artifacts: research ideation, candidate-code generation, reference-query planning, and manuscript assistance. Distinguish these from the numerical evaluator. Do not invent provider/model identities, human oversight or paid-API experiments; this is process provenance, not a numerical result.\n\nGrounding IDs: process provenance only; no numerical source ID claimed.\n\n## Writer contract: body budget, output, and limitations\n\n1. Scope: this strategy writes neither paper.tex nor claims_grounding.json, drafts no final paper, renders no figures, runs no new experiment, and invokes no final-paper validation. Dotted JSON fields, internal selection terms and hashes in this memo are private-only source maps, not visible manuscript labels. Memory is qualitative planning context only.\n\n2. Venue/layout: use VENUE.md and the supplied ICLR 2026 style. The inspected paper.sty has textwidth=5.5 inches and textheight=9 inches, single-column: column width equals full text width. All three figures use this text block, not a two-column figure* layout. Keep margins and typography unchanged.\n\n3. Body budget, approximately 8.5 pages including figures/tables but excluding references: title/abstract 0.5; introduction 1.0; related work 0.6; method 1.6; data/metrics/uncertainty protocol 1.1; results 2.6; discussion/limitations 0.8; conclusion 0.3. These are planned page equivalents, not measured pagination. Venue requires 8–9 body pages; an eight-page body must end at least 75% full. Spend space on scientific explanation, not padding or unsupported experiments.\n\n4. Thesis-first headings: Introduction; Related Work; Frozen-Prefix Ranking Audits; Data, Metrics, and Uncertainty; Dataset- and Budget-Dependent Disruption; Discussion and Limitations; Conclusion. Use three figures plus two compact tables: final aggregate metrics with seed-interval interpretation, and descriptive search configurations. Keep search context brief and distinct from final evidence.\n\n---TOOLS---\n/opt/autoillustrate-venv\n/opt/drawio\n/opt/headless\n/tmp/node-compile-cache\n/tmp/opencode\n/usr/local/lib/libpython3.12.so\n/usr/local/lib/libpython3.12.so.1.0\n/usr/local/lib/libpython3.so\n/usr/local/lib/node_modules\n/usr/local/lib/pkgconfig\n/usr/local/lib/python3.12\n/usr/local/lib/python3.13\n\n---VALIDATORS---\n/opt/autoillustrate-venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/openai/types/responses/tool_choice_apply_patch_param.py\n/opt/autoillustrate-venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/openai/types/responses/tool_choice_apply_patch.py\n/opt/autoillustrate-venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/openai/types/responses/response_apply_patch_tool_call_output.py\n/opt/autoillustrate-venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/openai/types/responses/response_apply_patch_tool_call.py\n/opt/autoillustrate-venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/openai/types/responses/apply_patch_tool_param.py\n/opt/autoillustrate-venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/openai/types/responses/apply_patch_tool.py\n/opt/autoillustrate-venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/openai/types/responses/__pycache__/tool_choice_apply_patch_param.cpython-312.pyc\n/opt/autoillustrate-venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/openai/types/responses/__pycache__/tool_choice_apply_patch.cpython-312.pyc\n/opt/autoillustrate-venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/openai/types/responses/__pycache__/response_apply_patch_tool_call_output.cpython-312.pyc\n/opt/autoillustrate-venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/openai/types/responses/__pycache__/response_apply_patch_tool_call.cpython-312.pyc\n/opt/autoillustrate-venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/openai/types/responses/__pycache__/apply_patch_tool_param.cpython-312.pyc\n/opt/autoillustrate-venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/openai/types/responses/__pycache__/apply_patch_tool.cpython-312.pyc\n\n---LOCAL MEMORY---\n- summary: Grounded six-query plan written; audit memory synchronized through canonical global paths after symlink-safe helper rejected global_memory; gate=kept; trigger=none; reason=Planning narrows literature scope without changing experimental recommendations.\n- evidence: reference_query_plan.json and reference_query_plan.md target Bradley-Terry, influence functions, finite-sample removal robustness, actual Arena/NBA data and allowed vote-rigging context. paper_data.json final evidence supersedes proposed MT-Bench comparisons: fixed-mask bootstrap disagreement gains differ in sign across Arena and NBA, and shortlist expansion tied the search aggregate. Generic optimization, architecture transfer, unexecuted judge comparisons and broad leaderboard-deletion searches were rejected as irrelevant, unsupported or unsafe. No bibliography, provenance, manuscript or claim-grounding files written and no retrieval performed.\n- next_action: Validate schema, six unique queries, output consistency and forbidden-output absence; later retrieve only exact allowed identities with no citation traversal.\n\n### 2026-11-17T22:32:29.715343+00:00 | step=final | scope=paper\n- summary: reference_query_plan_ready; gate=kept; trigger=none; reason=Validation confirms planning artifacts only and adds no experimental conclusion.\n- evidence: Passed JSON contract, six-query uniqueness and category checks, verbatim memo-query agreement, final five-seed/family/sign checks, memory synchronization and absence of forbidden outputs. Global memory helper required canonical paths because global_memory is a symlink; existing history preserved. No network requests, retrieval or experimental execution performed.\n- next_action: Later resolve only the five explicitly allowed starter identities and pinned NBA dataset source; do not broaden queries or traverse citations. Preserve conditional and cross-design limitations in the paper.\n\n### 2026-11-17T22:37:25.158871+00:00 | step=paper | scope=paper\n- summary: Framing audit favors cross-setting deletion sensitivity with a fixed-mask uncertainty limitation; gate=kept; trigger=none; reason=This is a paper organization decision, not a new experimental recommendation.\n- evidence: Independent final.qualification sources report completed and qualified; downstream_study and study.* are absent. Final episodes cover Arena/NBA at three deletion budgets, repeated across five seeds and reversed-row controls. Fixed-mask group-bootstrap records are duplicated across episode exports, with disagreement-relative gains negative in Arena and positive in NBA. Selected six-contender implementation is linked by best_program_manifest; no prior manuscript or edit context was staged. ICLR style specifies one 5.5-inch text column and 9-inch text height. Bibliography retrieval includes irrelevant matches and lacks several exact planned identities.\n- next_action: Write thesis-first strategy and figure/layout budgets; exclude campaign-count and search-delta claims, causal design attribution, attack-reoptimized uncertainty and unsupported citations.\n\n### 2026-11-17T22:45:05.035373+00:00 | step=paper | scope=paper\n- summary: Ready strategy written: measured frozen-prefix ranking sensitivity with dataset/budget limits beats unsupported grouped-frontier and universal-method framings; gate=kept; trigger=none; reason=Framing and layout do not change experimental recommendations.\n- evidence: paper_strategy.json and paper_strategy.md specify the common question, six narrowly scoped method/control/configuration groups, three required full-text-width figures, a 8.5-page ICLR allocation, and substantive supplementary sections. Qualification remains completed/qualified from final.qualification.*. Search raw scores are descriptive only; no study.* campaign claims. Fixed-mask group resampling remains conditional and its essential opposite dataset signs stay in the main text. No prior manuscript/edit inputs were staged. Canonical apply_patch and system patch were unavailable; an attempted patch-wrapper call failed without writing files, then the two strategy outputs were written using the available Python filesystem interface.\n- next_action: Complete strategy-only verification and preserve literature/reproducibility limitations; later writer must follow the framing contract without drafting a search diary or overstating qualification.\n\n### 2026-11-17T22:45:21.958786+00:00 | step=final | scope=paper\n- summary: paper_strategy_ready; strategy-only checks passed; gate=kept; trigger=none; reason=Verification confirms the framing artifacts without adding an experimental conclusion.\n- evidence: Passed exact output-schema checks, all declared source-ID and implementation-path checks, final qualification agreement, unique bootstrap count/completion/sign checks, aggregate reconstruction from unpermuted cases, figure panel/category/series/font budgets, 8.5-page allocation, memo/JSON agreement, and absence of paper.tex/claims_grounding.json. No final-paper validator, new experiment, network retrieval, or figure generation ran. Local/global append-only memory updates preserved existing history.\n- next_action: Hand off the ready standalone strategy. Later drafting must verify exact allowed references, disclose staged raw-pipeline gaps and LLM roles, preserve conditional uncertainty and dataset-specific limitations, and implement the specified full-text-width figures.\n\n\n---EDIT CONTEXT---\n\n---STAGED INPUTS---\n_idea_generation\nattempts_history.jsonl\nbest_program_manifest.json\nconclusions.md\nconclusions_history.jsonl\nconclusions_other_workers.md\nevents.jsonl\nidea_generation_failures.jsonl\nideas\nideas_history.jsonl\nlatest_run_manifest.json\nmemory.jsonl\nmemory.md\nouter_state.json\ntask\n\n---BIBLIOGRAPHY---\n@Article{Bradley1952RANKAO,\n@Inproceedings{Ott1977AnIT,\n@Inproceedings{Ziegel1977AnIT,\n@Article{Bradley1952RankAO,\n@Inproceedings{Muth1999BasicSA,\n@Article{Dykstra1960RankAO,\n@Article{Bradley1954TheRA,\n@Article{Bradley1955RANKAO,\n@Article{Su2006OnAC,\n@Article{Bradley1964CorrigendumTR,\n@Article{Han2020ExplainingBB,\n@Article{Khanna2018InterpretingBB,\n@Article{Basu2019SecondOrderGI,\n@Article{Basu2019OnSG,\n@Article{Zhou2023SurvivalOT,\n@Article{Saunshi2022UnderstandingIF,\n@Article{Wang2020EfficientDA,\n@Article{Yu2025GZOOBN,\n@Article{Tatsat2025BeyondTB,\n@Article{Koizumi2024PerformanceOU,\n@Article{Zhang2023UnderstandingDG,\n@Article{O'Brien2024ImprovingBR,\n@Article{Fang2024DiffExplainerUB,\n@Article{Wang2024AnalyzingCP,\n@Article{Chiaroni2022SimplexCV,\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
